From 6247a1a8152aadf6db998eb6ff7d71434b490b28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:08:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rust-rounds): keep the owner's work spans on home (RR26)

paulgsc/some-ui#3250. The phone's work tracker sends each span's start and,
once the owner says how much of it they worked (all, part or none), its
close. `rust_work_span_event` keeps both, one row per event, append-only and
the subject's, and leaves with the account.

- POST /rust-work-spans/start: 201 added, 200 the same start again, 409
  another start under the span's id, 409 carrying `open` while another span
  is open (one open at a time per subject), 422 naming each refused field.
- POST /rust-work-spans/close: 201, 200 the same close again, 409 another
  close, 404 a span with no start, 422 for seconds that do not fit the span
  (at most its whole seconds, all of them for `all`, 0 for `none`) or a
  close before its start.
- GET /rust-work-spans?week=<id>: the week's spans folded (start plus close
  or null) and the span open now, whatever its week, so a second device can
  ask about it before starting another.

The table's triggers refuse an update, a delete while the account stands, a
second open span and a close with no start. Contract epoch 21.

